hints:
`&&` short-circuits, which gives exactly the stop behaviour you need:
```go
func walk[K cmp.Ordered](n *node[K], yield func(K) bool) bool {
	if n == nil {
		return true
	}
	return walk(n.left, yield) && yield(n.key) && walk(n.right, yield)
}
```
The classic bug is calling `walk(n.left, yield)` as a statement and ignoring its result: the walk then keeps going after a `break` and the range loop panics.
